{"term":"justify","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:607e4b6fa3b2ef9bf5","definition":"To provide an acceptable explanation for.","example":"How can you justify spending so much money on clothes?","pos":"verb","synonyms":["vindicate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["dexify","justifyingly","justifying space","overjustify","rejustify","self-justify","the ends justify the means","unjustify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0df5827ed7b9216c5d","definition":"To be a good reason behind a normally-unacceptable action; to warrant.","example":"Nothing can justify your rude behaviour last night.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["vindicate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["dexify","justifyingly","justifying space","overjustify","rejustify","self-justify","the ends justify the means","unjustify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2acd41260fa9ff5d47","definition":"To arrange (text) on a page or a computer screen such that the left and right ends of all lines within paragraphs are aligned.","example":"The text will look better justified.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["vindicate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["dexify","justifyingly","justifying space","overjustify","rejustify","self-justify","the ends justify the means","unjustify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:067cc39309cd2b2b8f","definition":"To absolve, and declare to be free of blame or sin.","example":"I cannot justify whom the law condemns.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["vindicate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["dexify","justifyingly","justifying space","overjustify","rejustify","self-justify","the ends justify the means","unjustify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f7d7567e143da4fb33","definition":"To give reasons for one’s actions; to make an argument to prove that one is in the right.","example":"She felt no need to justify herself for deciding not to invite him.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["vindicate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"reflexive","register":"reflexive","wordFamily":["dexify","justifyingly","justifying space","overjustify","rejustify","self-justify","the ends justify the means","unjustify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0a8401db25699f29b3","definition":"To prove; to ratify; to confirm.","example":"She is not dead at Tarsus, as she should have been,\nBy savage Cleon: she shall tell thee all;\nWhen thou shalt kneel, and justify in knowledge\nShe is thy very princess.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["vindicate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["dexify","justifyingly","justifying space","overjustify","rejustify","self-justify","the ends justify the means","unjustify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6ff842fbc28099daff","definition":"To show (a person) to have had a sufficient legal reason for an act that has been made the subject of a charge or accusation.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["vindicate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["dexify","justifyingly","justifying space","overjustify","rejustify","self-justify","the ends justify the means","unjustify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:17f0bc307574bea66b","definition":"To qualify (oneself) as a surety by taking oath to the ownership of sufficient property.","example":"J'USTIFYING BAIL, practice, is the production of bail in court, who there justify' themselves against the exception of the plaintiff.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["vindicate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["dexify","justifyingly","justifying space","overjustify","rejustify","self-justify","the ends justify the means","unjustify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈd͡ʒʌstɪfaɪ/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5e/En-us-justify.ogg/En-us-justify.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["dexify","justifyingly","justifying space","overjustify","rejustify","self-justify","the ends justify the means","unjustify"]}